# Cursor / Codex Rules — Delonix Meet

## What this project is
Self-hosted corporate video conferencing platform. Backend: Rust (axum 0.7, webrtc-rs, sqlx 0.7, tokio). Frontend: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite. Production software, multi-tenant, E2EE, server-side recording, AI meeting minutes.

## Rust patterns

### Handlers
```rust
// Standard handler pattern — always this shape
async fn my_handler(
    Extension(pool): Extension<PgPool>,
    Extension(state): Extension<Arc<AppState>>,
    Json(body): Json<MyRequest>,
) -> Result<impl IntoResponse, AppError> {
    // Use sqlx macros, not string queries
    let row = sqlx::query_as!(MyRow, "SELECT ...", param).fetch_one(&pool).await?;
    Ok(Json(row))
}
```

### Error handling
```rust
// Use AppError from error.rs — never unwrap() on user data
return Err(AppError::NotFound("resource not found".into()));
return Err(AppError::Forbidden("cross-org access denied".into()));
// The ? operator converts sqlx::Error to AppError automatically
```

### New module checklist
1. Create `server/src/new_module.rs`
2. Add `mod new_module;` to `main.rs`
3. Add routes to the axum router in `main.rs`
4. If new DB tables needed: create `server/migrations/NNNN_description.sql`

### NEVER
- `unwrap()` or `expect()` on user-controlled data in production paths
- Raw SQL string queries — always use `sqlx::query!` macros
- Return data across org boundaries — scope every query with org_id check
- Use reqwest 0.13 — workspace is pinned to 0.12 (rustls compat)

## TypeScript/React patterns

### Components
```tsx
// Standard functional component
export function MyComponent({ prop }: { prop: string }) {
  const { t } = useTranslation();
  return <div style={{ color: 'var(--text)' }}>{t('ns.key')}</div>;
}
```

### Room grid tiles
```tsx
// ALWAYS inline styles for tile dimensions — never CSS vars
// Background tabs throttle rAF; var() causes frozen transitions
style={{ width: `${tileW}px`, height: `${tileH}px` }}
```

### Adding i18n strings
1. Add key to `web/src/i18n.ts` in both `pt` and `en` objects
2. Use `t('namespace.key')` in components — never hardcode strings

### Adding a WS message type
1. Add variant to the union type in `signaling.ts`
2. Add matching arm in `signaling.rs` (Rust `match` on `msg.type`)
3. Both must change together — the protocol is bidirectional

## CSS rules
- Colors: always `var(--token-name)` — never hex
- Room: `.room-page` always dark (see end of styles.css) — never remove `!important` overrides
- Themes: add under `[data-theme="name"]` at end of styles.css
- Fonts: Space Grotesk / Instrument Sans / IBM Plex Mono — already loaded via @fontsource

## Security checklist (before any PR)
- [ ] All new endpoints rate-limited or behind auth middleware
- [ ] Org isolation: new queries scoped to `org_id` of authenticated user
- [ ] No `unwrap()` on external input
- [ ] New webhook/HTTP calls: SSRF guard applied (check `webhooks.rs::is_safe_host`)
- [ ] Cookie changes: `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict` preserved
- [ ] Room token: new WS endpoints verify room token before upgrading

## Competitive context (shape your suggestions)
This platform replaces Zoom/Teams/Meet for organizations with data sovereignty needs. Core features are parity; differentiators are: no cloud dependency, real E2EE, Rust performance, self-host without royalty. When suggesting features, consider what Zoom/Teams/Meet have AND what they lack.

## What NOT to suggest
- Migrating SFU to LiveKit or mediasoup (decided: stay with custom Rust SFU)
- Using OpenAI API directly (MoM pipeline uses Claude API OR Ollama — both configurable)
- Adding cloud storage (recordings stay on local disk by design)
- Removing E2EE opt-outs (E2EE is always on; server recording uses explicit key delegation)
- Upgrading reqwest to 0.13

## File map (most important files)
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `server/src/main.rs` | Bootstrap, router, AppState, cron jobs |
| `server/src/auth.rs` | Registration, login, JWT, cookie |
| `server/src/sfu.rs` | WebRTC SFU — RTP fan-out, simulcast, recording tee |
| `server/src/signaling.rs` | WS /ws — all in-room message handling |
| `server/src/recorder.rs` | RTP→IVF/OGG→ffmpeg→webm pipeline |
| `web/src/webrtc.ts` | SfuCall: PeerConnection, simulcast, screen share, QoS |
| `web/src/e2ee.ts` | Insertable Streams AES-256-GCM |
| `web/src/media.ts` | Background effects, transcription, recording |
| `web/src/pages/Room.tsx` | Full in-room UI (grid, controls, tools, whiteboard) |
| `web/src/styles/` | Design tokens as CSS custom properties |
